# data-models-relationships

Importance Score: 75/100

Core Data Models:

1. Inmate Records
- Central entity tracking individuals in custody 
- Linked to multiple cases and bond records
- Contains biometric and demographic data

2. Case Management
- Tracks warrant and case status
- Associates inmates with jurisdictions
- Links to bond eligibility rules

3. Bond Records
- Stores bond amounts and conditions
- Maintains payment status and history
- References authorizing agents

4. Agent Management 
- Stores agent credentials and jurisdictions
- Tracks agent availability and assignments
- Links to bond authorizations

5. Location Records
- Geofence definitions for check-ins
- Consent-based tracking data
- Associates locations with cases

Key Relationships:

1. Inmate -> Cases (1:Many)
- Single inmate can have multiple active cases
- Each case links to specific jurisdiction rules

2. Cases -> Bonds (1:Many)
- Cases may have multiple bond records
- Bond status tied to case status

3. Bonds -> Agents (Many:Many)
- Multiple agents can manage bond records
- Agents handle bonds across jurisdictions

4. Cases -> Locations (1:Many) 
- Check-in locations tied to specific cases
- Multiple approved check-in points per case

Relevant Files:
- app/db.py
- app/storage.py

